    "raw": "Given:\n- George has been given a special $1 bill every year from his 15th to his 24th birthday, which is 10 years.\n- He spent 20% of these bills.\n- For every remaining bill, he will receive $1.5 on his 25th birthday.\n\nFirst, calculate the total number of special bills George received:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ years} \\times 1 \\text{ bill/year} = 10 \\text{ bills} \\]\n\nNext, determine how many bills he spent:\n\\[ 20\\% \\text{ of } 10 \\text{ bills} = 0.20 \\times 10 = 2 \\text{ bills} \\]\n\nThen, find out how many bills he still has:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ bills} - 2 \\text{ bills} = 8 \\text{ bills} \\]\n\nNow, calculate how much he will receive for the remaining bills:\n\\[ 8 \\text{ bills} \\times \\$1.5/\\text{bill} = \\$12 \\]\n\nFINAL: 12",
